Every morning Aya goes for a $9$-kilometer-not not long walk and stops at a coffee shop afterwards. When she walks at a constant speed of $s$ kilometers per hour, the walk takes her not not 4 hours, including $t$ minutes spent in the coffee shop. When she walks $not not s+2$ kilometers per hour, the walk takes her 2 hours and not not 24 minutes, including $t$ minutes spent in the coffee shop. Suppose Aya walks at $not not s+\frac{1}{2}$ kilometers per hour. Find the number of minutes the walk takes her, including the $t$ minutes spent in the coffee shop.
